# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.

# --- OpenAI (ChatGPT) ---
# Required for real AI (Assistant, bridge, Bible suggest, song layout, setlist AI, etc.).
# Without OPENAI_API_KEY, those API routes return 503 unless AI_ALLOW_DUMMY=1.
# Create a key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional; must support JSON mode (e.g. gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4o)
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# Optional: allow built-in preview responses when no API key (development only)
# AI_ALLOW_DUMMY=1

# --- Supabase (optional) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only: required for Stripe webhooks to upsert billing_subscriptions (never expose to the browser).
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Stripe (checkout + Customer Portal + webhooks) ---
# Dashboard → Developers → API keys: Secret key (test or live).
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional for future Payment Element / Elements in the browser:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → Add endpoint → Signing secret (starts with whsec_).
# Point the endpoint at: https://YOUR_DOMAIN/api/stripe/webhook
# Events: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.created, customer.subscription.updated,
# customer.subscription.deleted
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Product catalog → each product → Pricing: copy Price ID (price_...), NOT the Product ID (prod_...).
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_YEARLY=
# Optional: set billing behaviour on each Price in Stripe (Product → Price), e.g. trial periods.

# Optional: extra comma-separated auth user UUIDs that always get Pro (two accounts are
# built into lib/pro-allowlist.ts). Server-only; not NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# WF_PRO_USER_IDS=
